<title>BULGARIA: Bulgaria to offer two T-bill issues Sept 16.</title>
<headline>Bulgaria to offer two T-bill issues Sept 16.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgaria's Finance Ministry will offer two T-bill issues with a total par of six billion levs, both dated September 18, at separate auctions on Monday, the Bulgarian National Bank (BNB) said.</p>
<p>One of the issues has a nine-month maturity and a floater coupon equal to the BNB's central interest rate for the period to maturity. The CIR is now set at 108 percent annually.</p>
<p>The issue was offered with no minimum acceptable price set in advance by the ministry, the BNB said in a statement.</p>
<p>The second issue is a 56-day discount one.</p>
<p>Details of the issues follow:</p>
<p> Issue number	BG 3017996029	BG 3018096001</p>
<p> Type		  Floater coupon     Discount</p>
<p> Par value	   3.0 bln levs	 3.0 bln levs</p>
<p> Auction date	Sept 16, 1996	Sept 16, 1996</p>
<p> Issue date	  Sept 18, 1996	Sept 18, 1996</p>
<p> Maturity date     June 18, 1997	Nov 13, 1996</p>
<p>-- Sofia Newsroom, (++359-2) 981 8569</p>
